WEBVTT

00:45.086 --> 00:48.673
I went to college for geophysics
but dropped out.

00:48.757 --> 00:50.800
After I was discharged from the army,

00:50.884 --> 00:53.428
I passed the exam
and started working at the KMA.

00:54.095 --> 00:56.389
I'm a Grade Seven
Severe Weather Forecaster.

01:01.895 --> 01:05.273
What do your parents do?

01:09.027 --> 01:10.612
He had a CT scan.

01:10.695 --> 01:13.364
I see a 3cm-sized lump in his right lung

01:13.448 --> 01:16.409
that could be a tumor.

01:17.410 --> 01:20.246
I think he should receive a biopsy.

01:25.960 --> 01:29.005
My mother passed away when I was seven.

01:31.341 --> 01:32.592
And my father…

01:37.597 --> 01:41.142
He used to work at construction sites,
but ever since he was injured,

01:42.477 --> 01:44.103
he hasn't been working.

01:50.777 --> 01:51.986
Oh, okay.

01:54.197 --> 01:55.490
I see.

02:04.624 --> 02:07.877
The rain said to the wind…

02:08.586 --> 02:11.047
BIOPSY CONSENT FORM

02:11.131 --> 02:12.841
For the biopsy,

02:12.924 --> 02:15.093
he needs to be admitted
for one to two days.

02:15.176 --> 02:18.221
Also, you need to sign here.

02:20.682 --> 02:22.684
PATIENT OR GUARDIAN SIGNATURE

02:34.028 --> 02:35.446
"You push."

02:36.823 --> 02:39.367
"And I'll pour."

02:49.085 --> 02:54.716
EPISODE 15
ENSEMBLE

02:58.845 --> 02:59.846
Where are you going?

02:59.929 --> 03:00.930
What?

03:02.140 --> 03:04.267
You're still here?

03:05.768 --> 03:08.354
You shouldn't be walking around.
Go back inside.

03:08.438 --> 03:11.232
Insurance companies
are so meticulous these days.

03:12.275 --> 03:15.028
They accused me
of self-inflicted injury and blackmail

03:15.111 --> 03:17.030
and called the police.

03:17.113 --> 03:18.364
"Self-inflicted injury and blackmail"?

03:18.448 --> 03:21.492
I was just walking down the street,

03:21.576 --> 03:24.287
and a car rammed into me.

03:27.874 --> 03:28.833
By the way,

03:30.335 --> 03:32.503
didn't Si-woo come with you?

03:32.587 --> 03:35.340
I had no time to call him.
I'll call him now.

03:35.423 --> 03:38.217
No. Don't bother him.

03:38.301 --> 03:41.679
I'll pay you for the hospital bills soon.

03:42.263 --> 03:44.974
So don't press Si-woo for money.

03:45.058 --> 03:46.434
Got it?

03:48.061 --> 03:51.189
The doctor says you need a biopsy.

03:53.441 --> 03:55.944
You're more naive than I thought.

03:56.027 --> 04:00.365
The hospital is doing that to make money.
Don't be fooled.

04:00.990 --> 04:03.284
A CT scan showed something in your lung.

04:03.368 --> 04:05.078
When you get old,

04:05.161 --> 04:08.581
you're bound to have a few lumps.

04:13.211 --> 04:14.671
Did you already know?

04:17.924 --> 04:21.803
Well, if you have cash,
give me 10,000 won.

04:22.720 --> 04:25.223
I want to get some rice and soup.

04:30.270 --> 04:31.688
To get the biopsy done,

04:31.771 --> 04:34.190
you need to be admitted to the hospital.

04:37.277 --> 04:38.820
You should have it done.

04:39.654 --> 04:41.114
It's up to you though.

04:41.739 --> 04:43.491
There's no need to tell Si-woo.

04:46.202 --> 04:47.787
You won't tell him, will you?

04:55.753 --> 04:56.838
Jeez.

04:58.214 --> 04:59.382
I'm sorry.

05:24.532 --> 05:25.742
What are you doing here?

05:29.662 --> 05:31.205
I'm just thinking.

05:31.956 --> 05:33.624
Why do you have to do that here?

05:34.751 --> 05:36.210
It's none of your business.

05:36.794 --> 05:37.754
By the way,

05:37.837 --> 05:40.798
I met that Lee Si-woo guy.

05:42.508 --> 05:43.968
Why did you see him?

05:44.510 --> 05:45.678
What did you talk about?

05:47.764 --> 05:49.140
Why do you want to know?

05:49.223 --> 05:50.975
You said you broke up.

05:52.727 --> 05:53.936
We did.

05:55.855 --> 05:57.231
I'm glad you did.

05:57.315 --> 05:59.901
Not all relationships
end up in marriage anyway.

06:00.401 --> 06:01.694
Rest up. You must be tired.

06:36.145 --> 06:37.814
Doors opening.

06:45.988 --> 06:47.323
Doors closing.

07:37.957 --> 07:40.501
While the early cold continues,

07:40.585 --> 07:43.629
the first frost
was observed in Seoul today.

07:43.713 --> 07:45.965
As the temperature has fallen sharply,

07:46.048 --> 07:51.137
the current temperature in Seoul is 3°C
and the sensible temperature is 0.7°C.

07:51.220 --> 07:54.765
The KMA predicts that the weather
will be chilly until this evening

07:54.849 --> 07:59.020
and then recover to normal temperature
tomorrow afternoon.

07:59.604 --> 08:01.856
However, in the case
of the central region,

08:01.939 --> 08:04.484
the wind will blow rather strongly
from noon tomorrow.

08:04.567 --> 08:07.111
Please be mindful of facility management.

08:07.195 --> 08:10.865
The air is clean, and the average
daily fine dust concentration

08:10.948 --> 08:13.242
across the country
is at a level of normal to good.

08:13.326 --> 08:17.079
In the distant sea
in the central part of the East Sea--

08:20.958 --> 08:24.378
If it's too much for you,
I'll go to the hospital alone.

08:28.799 --> 08:30.343
Why won't you say anything?

08:31.552 --> 08:33.304
What we talked about yesterday…

08:35.056 --> 08:37.016
Can you give me some time
to think about it?

08:38.184 --> 08:39.977
If we miss the timing,

08:40.061 --> 08:41.562
we won't be able to do it.

08:47.777 --> 08:50.571
I really don't think
we can afford to have a baby now.

08:52.281 --> 08:54.075
Think about how much it'll cost.

08:54.700 --> 08:57.203
The hospital, childbirth,
and postnatal care center.

08:57.286 --> 08:59.205
If we move to a cheaper place,

09:00.122 --> 09:02.333
we'll be able to pay for them somehow.

09:02.416 --> 09:03.960
And then what?

09:09.507 --> 09:11.592
We have to raise the baby.

09:11.676 --> 09:13.386
Once my childbirth leave is over,

09:13.469 --> 09:15.596
we'll have to hire a nanny.

09:15.680 --> 09:17.473
I looked up how much they get paid

09:17.557 --> 09:19.725
and it's almost the same
as my starting salary.

09:22.979 --> 09:26.482
There are places like daycare centers.

09:27.233 --> 09:30.236
How can we send
a newborn baby to a daycare center?

09:34.490 --> 09:36.450
You go to work early in the morning,

09:36.534 --> 09:38.035
and I work overtime all the time.

09:38.619 --> 09:41.914
You could always take maternity leave.

09:44.709 --> 09:45.918
I can't do that.

09:46.002 --> 09:49.005
I took on my first regular column
since I started working.

09:49.088 --> 09:51.048
I don't want to lose this chance.

09:51.132 --> 09:52.925
I don't want to give up my career.

10:00.099 --> 10:02.893
We were so unprepared when we got married.

10:03.686 --> 10:06.647
So I want to be prepared
before I have a baby.

10:30.963 --> 10:32.340
Yes, what is it?

10:32.423 --> 10:33.466
Hi.

10:34.008 --> 10:36.552
The biopsy will be done in the afternoon.

10:36.636 --> 10:39.513
They need to do a blood test
and some other tests before that.

10:41.599 --> 10:42.600
I see.

10:43.267 --> 10:44.935
I have to fast starting from noon.

10:45.770 --> 10:47.772
If I had known that,

10:47.855 --> 10:50.024
I should have eaten a hearty breakfast.

10:50.107 --> 10:51.984
Jeez, I'm hungry.

10:52.068 --> 10:55.154
I'm on my way to work
and I have a meeting coming up.

10:55.946 --> 10:57.031
Wait.

10:58.199 --> 11:01.243
You haven't told Si-woo, right?

11:02.370 --> 11:04.038
I'm hanging up.

11:11.545 --> 11:14.507
NIGHT-DUTY ROOM

11:14.590 --> 11:17.635
What? Why were you in there?

11:17.718 --> 11:19.011
Did you stay up all night?

11:19.762 --> 11:22.014
No, I didn't.

11:22.098 --> 11:23.766
Haven't you found a place to live?

11:26.018 --> 11:28.312
Please don't tell Director Jin.

11:28.396 --> 11:30.815
Why not? Did you have a fight?

11:30.898 --> 11:33.526
No. I don't want her to worry about me.

11:34.276 --> 11:35.569
That's very touching.

11:36.904 --> 11:37.780
Get lost.

11:45.121 --> 11:46.622
Good morning.

11:47.289 --> 11:49.583
- Thanks for the hard work.
- You're here early.

11:49.667 --> 11:52.753
The weather is much colder
than I expected.

11:52.837 --> 11:54.046
It'll be okay.

11:54.130 --> 11:58.050
The continental anticyclone centered
in Siberia temporarily developed.

11:58.134 --> 12:00.010
But the warm air is strong in the south,

12:00.094 --> 12:01.470
so the cold will subside
tomorrow afternoon.

12:01.554 --> 12:03.556
How did the ensemble forecast
predictions come out?

12:03.639 --> 12:06.434
Ms. Lee, give me the ensemble predictions.

12:06.517 --> 12:08.602
ENSEMBLE FORECASTING: A METHOD
THAT MINIMISES ERRORS AND UNCERTAINTIES

12:08.686 --> 12:10.271
BY USING SEVERAL NUMERICAL MODELS
TO MAKE VARIOUS PREDICTIONS

12:10.354 --> 12:12.231
- Well…
- Here you go.

12:12.815 --> 12:16.318
The NWP model
and the ensemble predictions show that

12:16.402 --> 12:18.904
the temperature
will rise again tomorrow afternoon.

12:18.988 --> 12:19.989
They do.

12:20.072 --> 12:23.284
Yesterday's forecast notice
won't need to be revised much.

12:24.160 --> 12:26.871
Thanks to you,
I'll have it easy this time.

12:26.954 --> 12:28.497
You better be thankful.

12:35.629 --> 12:36.922
Good morning.

12:37.006 --> 12:39.133
- Hello.
- Good morning.

12:39.216 --> 12:40.217
Wait.

12:41.385 --> 12:43.137
You left this at my place yesterday.

12:43.846 --> 12:44.930
Oh…

12:46.474 --> 12:47.641
Right.

12:48.517 --> 12:50.311
I guess I was overwhelmed.

12:50.394 --> 12:53.063
My mom tends to do that to people.

12:55.608 --> 12:57.067
She said "mom."

13:04.033 --> 13:05.367
Let's talk later.

13:07.703 --> 13:08.954
Okay.

13:16.003 --> 13:17.838
He meets her mother now?

13:18.506 --> 13:20.966
That's great.

13:21.967 --> 13:23.344
Don't count your chickens yet.

13:23.427 --> 13:25.846
Things are going well.
Don't spoil the mood.

13:36.524 --> 13:37.650
Yes?

13:37.733 --> 13:39.068
Fasting…

13:39.652 --> 13:41.820
means I can't drink water too, right?

13:41.904 --> 13:44.615
I'm working. I'm sorry.

14:08.847 --> 14:10.349
Do you want coffee?

14:13.018 --> 14:14.103
Thanks.

14:33.122 --> 14:34.331
Well…

14:34.957 --> 14:37.877
when was the last time
you called your father?

14:40.379 --> 14:41.755
Why do you ask?

14:43.424 --> 14:46.844
Because the weather got cold
all of a sudden.

14:46.927 --> 14:49.054
I don't call him for things like that.

14:53.517 --> 14:56.395
Is it so difficult
to call him to say hello?

14:56.478 --> 14:58.355
It's not because it's difficult.

14:58.439 --> 14:59.732
It's because I don't want to.

15:02.651 --> 15:05.696
But he's old now.
Why don't you give him a call?

15:06.947 --> 15:09.199
My father isn't like other fathers.

15:09.283 --> 15:11.452
He has never cared about me

15:11.535 --> 15:14.330
or how I lived.

15:14.413 --> 15:16.540
So why should I care about him?

15:17.124 --> 15:20.502
Why do I have to call him
and see if he's doing all right?

15:20.586 --> 15:22.504
Cold weather isn't a big deal.

15:26.967 --> 15:28.427
Because you'll regret it.

15:30.804 --> 15:33.974
You're acting like this
because you're mad at him.

15:34.642 --> 15:38.437
But you might regret it later.

15:41.857 --> 15:45.319
You won't be able to do
anything about it then.

15:45.402 --> 15:46.445
No.

15:47.112 --> 15:49.073
I'll never regret anything.

15:50.115 --> 15:53.702
Because there isn't
a single moment I want to turn back

15:54.828 --> 15:56.163
regarding him.

16:10.928 --> 16:14.014
We quarreled because of his father.

16:15.557 --> 16:17.017
I didn't ask.

16:19.353 --> 16:20.479
Right.

16:23.565 --> 16:26.318
PART-TIME HOUSEKEEPER

16:28.862 --> 16:31.490
LOOKING FOR A PART-TIME HOUSEKEEPER

16:31.573 --> 16:33.158
HIRING FULL-TIME HOUSEKEEPERS

16:36.245 --> 16:40.249
DIAPER COSTS PER MONTH

16:48.632 --> 16:51.301
BABY FORMULA COST PER MONTH

17:16.660 --> 17:18.412
- Deputy Director Han.
- Yes?

17:19.580 --> 17:20.706
Aren't you going to eat?

17:21.749 --> 17:25.335
Well, I'm not that hungry.

17:25.419 --> 17:27.171
- You can go.
- Okay.

17:29.256 --> 17:31.967
Director, will you go for lunch?

17:32.718 --> 17:34.470
Is it lunchtime already?

17:35.137 --> 17:37.848
All right. Let's go have lunch.

17:38.432 --> 17:40.768
- Let's go, everyone.
- See you.

17:41.435 --> 17:44.229
I'm not hungry. You should go.

17:44.813 --> 17:46.356
- We'll get going then.
- Okay.

17:46.440 --> 17:48.358
Let's go for lunch.

17:48.442 --> 17:50.194
What should we have?

17:51.612 --> 17:53.405
All right.

18:02.331 --> 18:04.166
PARENTING COMMUNITY

18:08.212 --> 18:09.671
JOIN COMMUNITY

18:09.755 --> 18:11.548
SUBMIT INFORMATION TO JOIN COMMUNITY

18:11.632 --> 18:14.885
BABY BUMP NICKNAME

18:24.061 --> 18:25.187
Yes.

18:25.270 --> 18:28.357
Did you ask Bo-mi?

18:28.440 --> 18:30.692
Yes, I did.

18:30.776 --> 18:32.111
What does she want?

18:32.194 --> 18:34.363
- She wants to eat out.
- She wants to eat out?

18:34.905 --> 18:36.990
Doesn't she want a bag or clothes?

18:37.074 --> 18:39.493
No. She doesn't want them.

18:39.576 --> 18:41.703
She just wants to eat out with us.

18:41.787 --> 18:44.206
I barely remember the last time

18:44.289 --> 18:45.999
we all ate out together.

18:46.083 --> 18:47.251
She probably has no memory.

18:47.835 --> 18:50.003
It was when she was five or six.

18:50.504 --> 18:51.755
Right.

18:51.839 --> 18:55.384
Anyway, we went to a family restaurant
when she was a kindergartner.

18:55.467 --> 18:58.053
We ended up having a big fight though.

18:58.720 --> 19:00.597
Right. We did.

19:01.515 --> 19:05.102
I called the academy
and canceled her evening class,

19:05.185 --> 19:06.353
so book a restaurant.

19:06.436 --> 19:07.479
Okay.

19:07.980 --> 19:10.274
And tell me when and where to meet you.

19:10.858 --> 19:12.526
For your information, Bo-mi likes pasta.

19:12.609 --> 19:13.652
Pasta.

19:14.153 --> 19:15.571
Okay. Got it.

19:20.450 --> 19:23.078
Jeez, Um Dong-han.

19:23.162 --> 19:24.663
What have you been doing?

19:25.873 --> 19:28.417
I haven't done anything for them.

19:29.918 --> 19:30.752
Senior Forecaster Um.

19:30.836 --> 19:33.463
I printed out the ECMWF model data
and put it on your desk.

19:33.547 --> 19:35.215
You can read it before the meeting.

19:35.299 --> 19:36.633
I'll get the KIM ready too.

19:36.717 --> 19:38.343
Okay. Thanks.

19:46.935 --> 19:49.313
- Here's your citron tea.
- Thank you.

19:49.396 --> 19:50.898
One hot citron tea, please.

19:50.981 --> 19:53.483
Hi, Assistant Director Kim.
Long time no see.

19:53.567 --> 19:55.194
- Have you been well?
- Of course.

19:55.694 --> 19:57.237
It's so cold.

19:57.321 --> 20:00.032
Does it have to get cold so quickly?

20:00.115 --> 20:03.285
I know, right? Everything changes
so abruptly in this county.

20:04.411 --> 20:07.331
By the way, how is Ms. Kim
in your team doing?

20:07.915 --> 20:08.874
What?

20:11.543 --> 20:14.338
How many times have I told you that
comparing this with high-resolution data

20:14.421 --> 20:17.466
increases the likelihood
of unusual weather forecasts?

20:17.549 --> 20:19.551
You asked me to analyze the forecasts,

20:19.635 --> 20:21.929
but not to compare them.

20:25.557 --> 20:29.436
You've worked long enough
to know that you're supposed to.

20:31.063 --> 20:33.273
- I'm sorry.
- Do it again.

20:34.399 --> 20:35.525
Okay.

20:40.239 --> 20:42.991
What is it? Do you need help?

20:43.951 --> 20:45.160
No, it's okay.

20:52.251 --> 20:55.379
I heard that the Policy Division
is trying to get her on their team.

20:57.005 --> 20:58.465
Didn't you know?

21:03.095 --> 21:06.056
Cheer up. Drink this. It's citron tea.

21:07.224 --> 21:08.517
Thank you.

21:24.032 --> 21:25.033
Thanks.

21:31.456 --> 21:32.457
Director Jin.

21:32.958 --> 21:36.295
Don't you think the barometer
has a weird flow?

21:36.378 --> 21:37.337
What about it?

21:37.421 --> 21:40.215
Since the jet stream momentum
is maintained,

21:40.299 --> 21:44.011
it's unlikely that the upper cut-off low
will easily move to the east.

21:48.307 --> 21:49.558
According to the NWP model,

21:49.641 --> 21:52.519
the temperature will go back up
tomorrow afternoon.

21:52.602 --> 21:55.272
Yes, I know that.
Si-woo, come and look at this.

22:01.987 --> 22:03.864
Here. What do you think?

22:08.535 --> 22:10.787
It'd be better to analyze the possibility

22:10.871 --> 22:13.248
by comparing it with the live data.

22:13.332 --> 22:14.583
It's a bit strange, right?

22:14.666 --> 22:16.585
- Yes.
- What's strange about it?

22:16.668 --> 22:19.588
If you look here, the expansion
of the jet stream is too stable.

22:19.671 --> 22:22.049
We rarely had
a case like this before, right?

22:22.132 --> 22:24.134
Right. That's what bothers me.

22:27.971 --> 22:30.140
Among the ensemble prediction results,

22:30.223 --> 22:34.644
let's reanalyze the ensemble members
that are likely to prolong the cold wave.

22:35.312 --> 22:37.189
Okay. Then I'll proceed with the meeting

22:37.272 --> 22:39.649
based on the NWP model
that's been released.

22:39.733 --> 22:40.609
Okay.

22:41.443 --> 22:44.905
Assistant Director Shin. Can you send me
time series data for major regions?

22:44.988 --> 22:45.989
Okay.

22:51.161 --> 22:53.246
- I just sent it.
- Okay.

23:12.682 --> 23:14.184
How's your work going?

23:17.062 --> 23:18.522
It's not going well.

23:20.065 --> 23:21.358
Why not?

23:30.242 --> 23:32.452
Because it's so sunny.

23:37.415 --> 23:40.293
Last time, it wasn't going well
because it was cloudy.

23:41.753 --> 23:43.755
I guess she has low energy on a cold day.

23:45.298 --> 23:46.883
Can I help you with anything?

24:03.441 --> 24:05.402
Mom, I'm going out for a minute.

24:11.283 --> 24:12.576
Gosh, it's cold.

24:13.076 --> 24:15.829
Why didn't you tell me it was cold?

24:16.788 --> 24:18.331
Where's my down jacket?

24:18.415 --> 24:20.167
Mom! Where's my down jacket?

24:28.175 --> 24:32.220
You're 40 years old.
Why don't you look for it yourself?

24:32.304 --> 24:33.513
What's wrong, Mom?

24:34.014 --> 24:35.056
Are you mad at me?

24:35.140 --> 24:37.350
I have no energy to get mad at you.

24:37.434 --> 24:39.561
You and Ha-kyung
should take care of yourselves.

24:39.644 --> 24:41.605
Find your down jacket yourself.

24:51.823 --> 24:53.533
The average temperature across the country

24:53.617 --> 24:56.786
will drop by 10 to 15 degrees
as the cold air descends

24:56.870 --> 24:59.664
due to the continental
anticyclone development.

25:00.749 --> 25:01.875
All right.

25:01.958 --> 25:04.419
So when do you think
this cold will subside?

25:05.253 --> 25:08.340
Looking at the NWP model
and the ensemble forecast,

25:08.423 --> 25:11.843
it seems that the temperature will
normalize by tomorrow afternoon, but…

25:13.470 --> 25:15.305
"But"? But what?

25:17.349 --> 25:19.851
We found something strange
in the ensemble prediction,

25:19.935 --> 25:21.937
so we're analyzing it again.

25:23.021 --> 25:24.439
"Something strange"?

25:28.860 --> 25:30.028
ENSEMBLE PREDICTION

25:30.111 --> 25:33.198
Of the ensemble's thirty-two forecasts,
four models predicted that

25:33.281 --> 25:35.909
the cold wave
would last three days longer.

25:35.992 --> 25:40.163
Aren't we running the ensemble
to see which one is more likely?

25:40.247 --> 25:41.081
Yes…

25:41.748 --> 25:43.583
but this case is a bit different.

25:49.214 --> 25:51.383
A strong jet stream continues

25:51.466 --> 25:53.843
to be maintained
in the upper atmosphere at 10km.

25:53.927 --> 25:55.762
And the strong cut-off low

25:55.845 --> 25:58.974
at 5km is unable to move out to the east.

26:00.141 --> 26:02.686
You said only four
out of thirty-two were like this.

26:02.769 --> 26:05.522
Does that mean it will stay cold
for three to four more days?

26:05.605 --> 26:06.648
Yes.

26:08.108 --> 26:09.150
What do you want to do?

26:09.734 --> 26:10.610
As things stand--

26:10.694 --> 26:13.822
We may have to overturn the forecast.

26:32.007 --> 26:33.174
Forecaster Lee.

26:33.800 --> 26:36.136
Do you know what it means
to overturn the forecast?

26:37.387 --> 26:38.471
Yes, I do.

26:44.728 --> 26:46.354
Do you agree with him?

26:49.024 --> 26:50.275
Overturn the forecast?

26:50.358 --> 26:53.194
- No way.
- If it's wrong, there will be an uproar.

27:03.955 --> 27:05.040
Director Jin.

27:06.541 --> 27:07.834
Do you agree with him?

27:09.586 --> 27:10.920
Yes, I do.

27:30.106 --> 27:32.275
Yes, sir. I'm almost there.

27:32.359 --> 27:33.985
No, stop!

27:34.069 --> 27:36.863
Turn around and go back to the KMA.

27:36.946 --> 27:38.239
Why?

27:38.323 --> 27:40.575
I already sent you tomorrow's articles.

27:41.826 --> 27:45.372
The KMA is overturning the forecast.

27:45.455 --> 27:46.581
What?

27:49.584 --> 27:51.086
What are you going to do?

27:51.628 --> 27:53.630
How will you handle the aftermath?

27:54.214 --> 27:57.342
The entire Chief Team could turn on you.

27:57.425 --> 28:00.428
I can't ignore the numerical results
because of that.

28:00.512 --> 28:03.515
Looking at the ensemble value,
isn't the previous forecast correct?

28:03.598 --> 28:06.351
Senior Forecaster Um, Forecaster Lee,

28:07.018 --> 28:08.561
and I think it's reasonable.

28:09.312 --> 28:10.313
So…

28:10.397 --> 28:13.024
you're going to take the bullet
for what Si-woo said?

28:13.108 --> 28:14.484
You know,

28:14.567 --> 28:17.445
when I was younger,
whenever I caused trouble,

28:17.529 --> 28:21.324
Director Choi supported me
and covered for me.

28:23.201 --> 28:25.412
That's how I got here.

28:25.995 --> 28:29.040
Now, I want to do that
for my younger colleagues.

28:30.875 --> 28:33.628
We're at that age and position.

28:40.552 --> 28:42.095
I envy you.

28:43.054 --> 28:47.475
Because you act,
think, and talk like an adult.

28:50.228 --> 28:51.396
Are you making fun of me?

28:52.021 --> 28:54.691
No, I'm not. I really mean it.

28:54.774 --> 28:56.317
Why are you suddenly like this?

28:59.529 --> 29:01.489
I'm often like this these days.

29:02.449 --> 29:06.119
Nothing is free in this world.
You don't become an adult automatically.

29:07.829 --> 29:11.166
I have to be responsible
for so many things.

29:11.833 --> 29:13.543
It's really difficult

29:14.502 --> 29:16.004
to be an adult.

29:20.884 --> 29:22.135
All right.

29:22.218 --> 29:25.138
If the Chief Team wants to
overturn the forecast, so be it.

29:25.221 --> 29:27.390
We'll think about the aftermath later.

29:30.059 --> 29:31.978
I'll release the forecast, Director Jin.

29:32.061 --> 29:33.438
Thanks.

29:33.521 --> 29:34.606
Bye.

29:44.324 --> 29:47.118
SI-WOO'S FATHER

29:52.540 --> 29:54.375
Yes, what is it this time?

29:55.376 --> 29:57.504
Well, I just called

29:57.587 --> 30:00.089
because I'm getting the biopsy done soon.

30:00.715 --> 30:01.966
I see.

30:03.051 --> 30:04.302
Anyway…

30:05.887 --> 30:08.139
thanks for booking the ward too.

30:08.765 --> 30:11.142
I'm lucky to have such a good son.

30:11.226 --> 30:15.146
I'll put in a good word
for you with Si-woo.

30:15.730 --> 30:17.023
To be honest,

30:17.106 --> 30:19.984
you seem picky,
so you aren't exactly my type.

30:20.735 --> 30:24.948
Still, Si-woo has a better eye
for women than I do.

30:25.031 --> 30:26.199
Right?

30:26.991 --> 30:28.326
Actually…

30:29.327 --> 30:30.745
we broke up.

30:33.832 --> 30:35.333
You broke up?

30:35.416 --> 30:36.584
Why?

30:37.627 --> 30:39.170
Did Si-woo do something wrong?

30:39.754 --> 30:40.588
No.

30:40.672 --> 30:42.090
Then…

30:42.799 --> 30:44.467
Did he disobey you, Director Jin?

30:45.051 --> 30:46.052
No.

30:47.720 --> 30:48.805
That's weird.

30:49.305 --> 30:51.558
He'd never cheat on anyone

30:51.641 --> 30:53.351
or get drunk and fight.

30:54.102 --> 30:55.061
But did he?

30:55.937 --> 30:57.188
No, he didn't.

30:57.272 --> 30:58.898
Then why did you break up?

30:59.732 --> 31:02.235
And why are you good to me
when you've broken up?

31:03.069 --> 31:05.238
Why did you make me get the tests done,

31:05.321 --> 31:06.990
and reserve a ward for me?

31:07.615 --> 31:11.369
Because Forecaster Lee is still
a member of Chief Team Two.

31:11.953 --> 31:14.080
As his senior colleague and director,

31:14.163 --> 31:16.583
I can help you this much.

31:19.335 --> 31:22.297
You still have feelings for him,
don't you?

31:25.091 --> 31:26.551
I'm busy so I have to go.

31:26.634 --> 31:28.845
Good luck with your tests. Bye.

31:34.350 --> 31:36.394
What an idiot.

31:37.687 --> 31:39.772
He shouldn't have let her go.

31:42.859 --> 31:44.110
Jeez.

32:08.343 --> 32:09.469
Reporter Chae!

32:10.053 --> 32:12.555
What are you doing here? Are you ill?

32:13.932 --> 32:15.266
I just have a stomachache.

32:16.517 --> 32:17.477
Are you…

32:18.311 --> 32:19.312
What?

32:20.313 --> 32:21.397
Goodness.

32:25.026 --> 32:26.110
Is it constipation?

32:27.070 --> 32:29.197
It's all because of stress.

32:32.325 --> 32:34.202
Try this. It's a herb medicine.

32:34.285 --> 32:36.120
It works within an hour.

32:37.830 --> 32:39.540
Don't struggle.

32:39.624 --> 32:41.960
Get medicinal help when you need it.

32:42.043 --> 32:44.253
- All right?
- Okay.

32:44.337 --> 32:45.672
I'll go in first.

32:46.547 --> 32:47.382
See you.

32:57.642 --> 33:00.561
AREUM OBSTETRICS AND GYNECOLOGY
YOUR RESERVATION HAS BEEN CONFIRMED

33:12.949 --> 33:16.744
I'll give you a brief overview first,

33:16.828 --> 33:18.454
and then take questions.

33:24.669 --> 33:26.462
The cold wave that started yesterday

33:26.546 --> 33:29.841
is expected to continue
for three or four more days.

33:30.425 --> 33:34.303
The cold wave, which was initially
predicted to subside from tomorrow,

33:34.387 --> 33:37.265
is expected to continue
until this weekend,

33:37.348 --> 33:40.184
mainly in the central region
and some southern inland regions.

33:40.268 --> 33:41.728
- Bye.
- Good night.

33:41.811 --> 33:43.146
- See you.
- Bye.

33:44.272 --> 33:46.899
- I'm off. Bye.
- Bye.

34:00.830 --> 34:02.165
Aren't you going home?

34:02.248 --> 34:04.167
Go ahead. I want to monitor it a bit more.

34:52.048 --> 34:53.174
Thanks.

34:56.511 --> 34:58.471
Will the jet stream hold up?

34:58.554 --> 35:00.431
Only the current knows

35:00.515 --> 35:02.308
whether it'll hold out or retreat.

35:02.391 --> 35:04.227
The forecast has been released.

35:04.310 --> 35:06.521
So stop monitoring and go home.

35:06.604 --> 35:09.315
I'll stay here a little longer.

35:16.114 --> 35:19.826
- Earlier--
- I'm sorry about what happened earlier.

35:21.202 --> 35:23.538
You were probably
just asking how he was doing,

35:23.621 --> 35:24.997
but I overreacted.

35:28.626 --> 35:30.253
You're right.

35:30.336 --> 35:32.255
Whenever we talk about my father,

35:32.338 --> 35:34.173
I act like a kid.

35:34.257 --> 35:37.635
I try not to be like that,
but I can't help it.

35:38.845 --> 35:40.721
It's always been that way.

35:41.305 --> 35:43.224
My relationships started with love

35:44.475 --> 35:45.726
but my father

35:46.894 --> 35:48.729
was always at the end of them.

35:51.482 --> 35:55.736
He's a difficult person to deal with,
even for me. I'm sick of him.

35:56.320 --> 35:58.322
I didn't want to burden

35:58.406 --> 36:01.826
the woman I love
by making my father her family.

36:04.287 --> 36:06.289
Isn't being in love enough?

36:07.582 --> 36:10.168
Is it necessary to become a family?

36:11.335 --> 36:12.962
But the world tells you that

36:13.754 --> 36:16.257
you should take responsibility
for loving someone

36:16.340 --> 36:19.135
and that the only way
to do that is through marriage.

36:19.760 --> 36:20.970
So…

36:23.181 --> 36:24.765
I told her we should break up.

36:49.540 --> 36:50.750
I'm sorry.

36:56.172 --> 36:59.091
It's okay.
You don't have to apologize to me.

36:59.884 --> 37:01.093
I understand.

37:06.390 --> 37:08.559
I really do. I understand.

37:16.234 --> 37:17.568
Si-woo.

37:19.111 --> 37:21.239
Why do you keep saying it's okay?

37:22.031 --> 37:23.366
Why do you keep saying

37:24.617 --> 37:25.868
that you understand me?

37:30.373 --> 37:33.960
What will you do
if I beg you to come back?

37:36.545 --> 37:38.214
What will you do

37:39.006 --> 37:40.883
if I say I can't break up with you?

37:51.477 --> 37:52.853
I still…

37:54.855 --> 37:56.816
like you a lot.

37:59.902 --> 38:01.028
Do you know that?

38:09.620 --> 38:11.998
Hey! Where is Director Jin Ha-kyung?

38:12.581 --> 38:14.250
Hey, Director Jin!

38:20.006 --> 38:21.424
Director Jin!

38:21.924 --> 38:24.135
Director Jin Ha-kyung!

38:24.218 --> 38:25.219
We'll talk later.

38:29.682 --> 38:31.434
Hey, where's Director Jin?

38:31.517 --> 38:34.395
Did she go home
after messing up the forecast?

38:34.478 --> 38:36.939
Where did Director Jin go?

38:37.023 --> 38:38.274
I'm here, sir.

38:38.816 --> 38:42.653
Hey, who told you
to overturn the forecast?

38:42.737 --> 38:44.030
How dare you!

38:44.113 --> 38:46.407
There's no sign
of the jet stream retreating

38:46.490 --> 38:48.659
in the upper atmosphere at 10km.

38:48.743 --> 38:49.785
Hey.

38:50.411 --> 38:53.122
We analyze based on the forecast
of the previous team

38:53.205 --> 38:55.666
not because we're dumb,
but because their forecast,

38:55.750 --> 38:58.753
which they analyzed by comparing
the data values with the live situation

38:58.836 --> 39:01.047
for 12 hours, is the most reliable source.

39:01.130 --> 39:03.215
But you overturn the forecast
without respect to that?

39:03.299 --> 39:05.217
It's not that I don't respect it.

39:05.301 --> 39:07.553
I simply forecasted
based on the live situation.

39:07.636 --> 39:09.680
What if your forecast is wrong?

39:09.764 --> 39:11.724
Who will deal with the consequences?

39:11.807 --> 39:13.434
Human cost and material expenses.

39:13.517 --> 39:15.102
Who will be responsible for those?

39:15.186 --> 39:17.730
But unusual weather has been observed.

39:17.813 --> 39:19.106
Should I keep my mouth shut

39:19.190 --> 39:21.275
just because of
a senior colleague's forecast?

39:21.359 --> 39:22.401
What?

39:29.033 --> 39:31.285
HEADQUARTERS
SHIN SEOK-HO

39:31.369 --> 39:32.828
Hi, Assistant Director Shin.

39:33.496 --> 39:35.456
Where are you, Senior Forecaster Um?

39:36.040 --> 39:39.251
I think you need to
come back to the office.

39:39.335 --> 39:41.504
Why? What's going on?

39:41.587 --> 39:43.297
The director of Chief Team One

39:43.381 --> 39:45.424
is furious because
of the overturned forecast.

39:45.508 --> 39:47.635
What did you just say?

39:49.095 --> 39:51.055
Say that again.

39:51.138 --> 39:52.348
Say that again!

39:54.475 --> 39:55.518
What did you just say?

39:55.601 --> 39:57.269
- What did you say?
- Director.

39:57.353 --> 39:58.854
- Stop it, guys.
- What did you say?

39:58.938 --> 40:01.357
- Today's my daughter's birthday.
- Please calm down.

40:01.440 --> 40:04.068
- Let me eat out with my family.
- Jin Ha-kyung!

40:04.151 --> 40:07.029
- What did you just say?
- What are you doing?

40:07.113 --> 40:09.407
- Who are you?
- You can talk to me.

40:09.490 --> 40:12.118
Do you think I'm a joke
because you're all that?

40:12.201 --> 40:14.787
Admit that you were wrong and apologize.

40:14.870 --> 40:15.996
Apologize to me now!

40:18.499 --> 40:22.128
I didn't do anything wrong, sir.

40:23.712 --> 40:25.423
What? Jeez.

40:25.506 --> 40:28.717
Hey, you've come a long way. How dare you?

40:28.801 --> 40:30.511
- Please stop--
- Get off me!

40:30.594 --> 40:33.597
I'll show you how strict
and disciplined Chief Team should be.

40:33.681 --> 40:35.266
What did you say to me?

40:35.349 --> 40:36.851
- Let go of her!
- Say it again.

40:36.934 --> 40:38.185
- Let go!
- Don't you have any respect?

40:38.269 --> 40:40.229
- Don't you?
- I said let go of her!

41:00.791 --> 41:02.251
SENIOR FORECASTER UM DONG-HAN

41:02.334 --> 41:03.377
Hello?

41:05.004 --> 41:06.422
What was that?

41:07.089 --> 41:08.132
Seok-ho.

41:10.301 --> 41:11.343
Seok-ho?

41:17.892 --> 41:19.393
Hey, Si-woo.

41:27.485 --> 41:30.029
I knew something like this would happen.

41:34.533 --> 41:37.536
Yes, Director General. This is Sung-jin.

41:37.620 --> 41:38.871
Oh, no.

41:48.130 --> 41:49.089
Damn it.

42:01.644 --> 42:04.355
It isn't like Dad
to reserve a place like this.

42:05.648 --> 42:07.733
It's because you said
you wanted to eat out.

42:08.400 --> 42:09.902
This is a really popular place.

42:10.528 --> 42:12.154
I looked it up on social media.

42:12.238 --> 42:13.697
Celebrities come here.

42:14.198 --> 42:16.659
It's the hottest place in Cheongdam-dong.

42:17.284 --> 42:19.119
They say it's hard to get a reservation.

42:19.203 --> 42:22.373
Really? It's really not like your dad.

42:22.456 --> 42:24.333
I guess he put some effort into it.

42:26.877 --> 42:29.004
What should we get?

42:36.178 --> 42:37.763
BO-MI'S DAD

42:49.316 --> 42:51.068
Hi. What is it? Where are you?

42:51.151 --> 42:52.361
I…

42:53.153 --> 42:55.072
was really on my way there.

42:55.155 --> 42:57.032
But I'm sorry.

42:57.116 --> 42:59.910
I suddenly got a call from the KMA.

42:59.994 --> 43:02.162
- Okay. I got it.
- Hyang-rae, I…

43:02.246 --> 43:03.747
- I'll--
- I got it. Bye.

43:12.047 --> 43:14.341
What's wrong?
Did Dad say he can't make it?

43:17.720 --> 43:20.347
Yes. I don't know why

43:21.557 --> 43:23.642
he always does this on a day like this.

43:24.852 --> 43:27.396
- What should we do?
- Let's just eat.

43:31.400 --> 43:33.485
Can I order two dishes?

43:33.569 --> 43:35.446
When else will I get to come here?

43:45.748 --> 43:48.167
You're a habitual offender, aren't you?

43:49.418 --> 43:51.378
It was a mistake, sir.

43:51.462 --> 43:54.548
He was trying to break up a fight.
It was by accident.

43:55.424 --> 43:57.551
You started it first, sir.

43:57.635 --> 44:01.263
Forecaster Lee was only trying to
stop you. It was an accident.

44:02.640 --> 44:03.932
An accident?

44:04.016 --> 44:05.351
Forecaster Lee.

44:05.434 --> 44:07.811
I'm sure this wasn't
your first time hitting someone.

44:08.395 --> 44:11.815
I heard you punched
Han Ki-jun at the Office of Spokesperson.

44:11.899 --> 44:13.817
Take it out on me,

44:13.901 --> 44:15.986
not on everyone in Chief Team Two.

44:16.070 --> 44:17.404
Hey, Ha-kyung.

44:17.488 --> 44:19.907
Worry about the forecast
before you worry about them.

44:19.990 --> 44:22.451
What will you do
if your forecast is wrong?

44:22.534 --> 44:25.871
What do you want me to do? Should I quit?

44:26.747 --> 44:28.082
Did you say "quit"?

44:28.165 --> 44:29.792
Sir, please calm down.

44:29.875 --> 44:31.877
But if our forecast is right,

44:31.960 --> 44:34.129
you better quit your job, Director Choi.

44:34.213 --> 44:36.298
- What?
- Is this Squid Game?

44:36.382 --> 44:37.883
Why does anyone have to quit
if they get it wrong?

44:37.966 --> 44:40.761
Let's put our jobs on the line.

44:40.844 --> 44:44.306
It'll go down in KMA history,
and make a nice lesson.

44:44.390 --> 44:45.391
What do you say? Are you in?

44:45.474 --> 44:47.059
How dare you!

44:47.142 --> 44:48.477
Stop it!

44:48.560 --> 44:51.063
Jeez. That's enough.

44:51.146 --> 44:54.024
Why are you fighting?
Did you get a nosebleed?

44:56.944 --> 44:58.654
What are you doing?

44:58.737 --> 45:03.117
You're decent people. Why are you
hitting each other and fighting?

45:04.034 --> 45:05.369
I didn't hit him.

45:05.953 --> 45:07.913
I hit him.

45:08.497 --> 45:09.790
It was an accident.

45:09.873 --> 45:11.750
It was clearly a mistake.

45:12.876 --> 45:14.628
Three of them came at me.

45:15.254 --> 45:18.173
Let me make myself clear.
I was only trying to stop them.

45:20.134 --> 45:22.636
Whatever. Senior Forecaster Um.

45:22.719 --> 45:24.805
What did you teach your juniors?
Why are they a mess?

45:24.888 --> 45:26.432
Weather is about flow.

45:26.515 --> 45:29.435
Didn't I tell you that
you can't overturn it with a few numbers?

45:29.518 --> 45:31.937
But just because
a few ensemble predictions

45:32.020 --> 45:33.772
came out differently,

45:33.856 --> 45:36.233
you overturned the forecast that was based

45:36.316 --> 45:37.568
on a week's worth
of analysis by four teams.

45:37.651 --> 45:38.986
What?

45:39.069 --> 45:41.738
You've overturned my forecast before.

45:42.239 --> 45:44.116
- Have I?
- Did he?

45:44.199 --> 45:45.159
Twice at that.

45:46.410 --> 45:47.744
Twice?

45:48.954 --> 45:50.164
When?

45:50.247 --> 45:52.541
During the summer
heatwave warning in 2004,

45:52.624 --> 45:54.376
and in 2011 when the temperature
was abnormally low.

45:54.460 --> 45:55.627
You and I were right once each.

45:55.711 --> 45:57.754
But even when you were wrong,

45:57.838 --> 46:00.048
I didn't say anything about it.

46:00.132 --> 46:01.467
Because…

46:01.550 --> 46:04.553
I trusted you
for having such a strong conviction.

46:05.220 --> 46:09.725
Aren't you her senior?
Why can't you trust your junior colleague?

46:09.808 --> 46:13.145
Are you throwing a tantrum
because your forecast was overturned?

46:13.228 --> 46:17.441
It's because this brat ignored me
and lashed out at me.

46:17.524 --> 46:18.567
Director Choi.

46:19.401 --> 46:21.153
She's the director of Chief Team Two.

46:22.488 --> 46:24.198
She's on the same level as you.

46:24.281 --> 46:27.743
She has as much authority
and responsibility as you do.

46:28.744 --> 46:30.746
You should be ashamed of yourself.

46:30.829 --> 46:32.539
Stop being a preachy boomer.

46:32.623 --> 46:33.999
How can you speak to her like that?

46:34.082 --> 46:35.501
Where are your manners?

46:40.631 --> 46:42.799
It's because I'm angry! Is that so wrong?

46:42.883 --> 46:45.219
Why would you get so mad over this?

46:45.302 --> 46:47.846
I should be the one who's furious!

46:47.930 --> 46:50.015
Today's my daughter's birthday!

46:50.098 --> 46:53.268
For the first time in ten years,
I was going to eat out

46:53.352 --> 46:55.145
with my kid and my wife.

46:55.229 --> 46:56.563
I even did my hair

46:56.647 --> 46:59.399
and booked a restaurant.
I was going to be a good dad today.

46:59.483 --> 47:01.401
They must have finished eating by now!

47:08.325 --> 47:12.204
The pressure difference
in Siberia is falling sharply.

47:18.794 --> 47:19.628
Ms. Lee.

47:19.711 --> 47:23.674
Trace the development
of the global model over time.

47:23.757 --> 47:24.675
Jeez.

47:28.679 --> 47:30.430
The jet stream is moving south.

47:31.181 --> 47:32.266
What…

47:32.975 --> 47:35.394
Why is it moving down?

47:35.477 --> 47:36.645
Damn it.

47:41.275 --> 47:43.360
What are you doing? Go home.

47:44.736 --> 47:46.071
Go home already.

48:19.271 --> 48:20.564
Doors opening.

48:22.316 --> 48:23.817
- Hello.
- Hello.

48:30.741 --> 48:32.075
Doors closing.

48:40.626 --> 48:41.793
Ki-jun.

48:44.087 --> 48:46.465
You finished late.
Did you just send the manuscript?

48:47.257 --> 48:48.175
Yes.

48:48.675 --> 48:50.844
It took me longer
because I wasn't feeling well.

48:56.975 --> 49:00.228
You looked unwell during the briefing,
so I was worried.

49:01.730 --> 49:03.190
Are you still sick?

49:03.857 --> 49:05.525
No, I'm fine.

49:10.530 --> 49:11.865
I thought about it, Yu-jin.

49:13.742 --> 49:14.993
The baby…

49:17.204 --> 49:18.121
I welcome it.

49:24.211 --> 49:25.379
I'm…

49:26.338 --> 49:28.173
not ready to be a dad,

49:30.425 --> 49:33.845
so I'll probably be flustered
and get confused often

49:34.429 --> 49:35.847
after the baby is born.

49:35.931 --> 49:38.642
I might act like an idiot in many ways.

49:40.185 --> 49:42.020
But still, it's our baby,

49:43.105 --> 49:44.815
so I want to do my best to raise it.

49:47.567 --> 49:49.861
- Ki-jun, I--
- But…

49:50.529 --> 49:53.573
if you still aren't sure
about having this baby,

49:55.033 --> 49:56.868
I'll respect your decision.

49:58.870 --> 50:01.790
I can't force you
to make sacrifices alone.

50:06.128 --> 50:07.337
The only thing

50:07.421 --> 50:10.590
I can say to you now is

50:10.674 --> 50:12.843
that whatever decision you make,

50:13.593 --> 50:15.554
I'll be with you.

50:16.596 --> 50:20.142
I'll be by your side,

50:21.935 --> 50:23.353
so you will never be lonely.

50:33.155 --> 50:34.906
I'm hungry. Aren't you?

50:35.532 --> 50:37.075
Should we grab something to eat?

51:53.276 --> 51:54.945
You made all this?

51:55.654 --> 51:59.157
I made them with the ingredients I had.

51:59.241 --> 52:00.700
It smells great.

52:00.784 --> 52:03.870
I'm a good cook like my mother.

52:16.758 --> 52:18.093
Tae-kyung.

52:18.677 --> 52:20.720
Is there anything you can't do?

52:21.429 --> 52:24.015
You can draw, cook,
and you have a great personality.

52:25.308 --> 52:26.142
Really?

52:28.436 --> 52:30.647
You're good at everything
except writing a story.

52:38.280 --> 52:40.031
What about my story writing?

52:40.115 --> 52:42.075
Is it boring?

52:42.158 --> 52:44.995
No, it's not that. How should I say this?

52:45.078 --> 52:46.663
It's not bad.

52:46.746 --> 52:50.333
It just doesn't have
a hooking point that draws you in.

52:51.710 --> 52:55.088
A hooking point?

52:55.171 --> 52:59.467
But you're good at
drawing cute characters.

53:08.310 --> 53:11.771
That means my story is bad
because it has no hooking point.

53:13.148 --> 53:17.235
No. I don't think I said it was bad.

53:17.319 --> 53:19.237
And my books don't sell.

53:19.821 --> 53:21.323
I don't think I said that.

53:21.406 --> 53:24.784
Isn't it implied contextually
because it has no hooking point?

53:31.625 --> 53:34.336
Shall we have some wine?

53:34.961 --> 53:37.047
- Do you want some?
- No.

53:38.340 --> 53:39.758
Let's continue our talk.

53:48.558 --> 53:50.018
Doors opening.

53:53.855 --> 53:55.649
- Doors closing.
- All right.

54:03.239 --> 54:04.199
What?

54:14.501 --> 54:17.420
Did she change the passcode?

54:29.432 --> 54:31.267
Did you change the passcode?

54:31.851 --> 54:35.146
Yes, I did. Because I need privacy.

54:35.230 --> 54:38.191
Stop talking nonsense.
Give me the new passcode.

54:39.109 --> 54:41.653
I'm sorry, Mom. You should go home.

54:46.533 --> 54:47.909
Why didn't you tell her?

54:48.493 --> 54:50.078
It's cold.

54:50.912 --> 54:53.206
It's okay. She's tougher than you think.

55:01.172 --> 55:04.384
By the way, where are we going?

55:07.095 --> 55:08.054
To a hospital.

55:10.515 --> 55:12.642
She's so heartless.

55:13.560 --> 55:16.563
I don't understand why she's so cold.

55:17.439 --> 55:18.565
Goodness.

55:19.190 --> 55:22.986
What am I going to do with these?
I can't bring them back.

55:32.746 --> 55:33.913
Tell me.

55:33.997 --> 55:38.001
Tell me which part of the story
you don't like specifically.

55:38.084 --> 55:41.588
Well, it's not that I don't like it…

55:42.547 --> 55:44.632
Why do you keep changing your mind?

55:44.716 --> 55:48.428
You clearly said my story
didn't have a hooking point.

55:48.511 --> 55:50.472
Well, a hooking…

55:51.389 --> 55:54.017
You're more persistent than I thought.

55:55.435 --> 55:58.772
How could one be a writer
if she's not persistent?

55:58.855 --> 56:00.899
I spend a long time drawing, writing,

56:00.982 --> 56:03.818
erasing, correcting,
contemplating and creating.

56:03.902 --> 56:06.905
Seok-ho, have you ever stayed up all night

56:06.988 --> 56:08.823
trying to think of a word?

56:09.949 --> 56:11.910
In order to write a single line,

56:11.993 --> 56:14.037
I keep thinking, writing,

56:14.120 --> 56:17.165
and rewriting all week
until my head is about to explode.

56:17.248 --> 56:19.042
I write and rewrite every word

56:19.125 --> 56:21.211
and every ending thousands of times.

56:21.294 --> 56:23.755
I constantly think about
how to make better sentences

56:23.838 --> 56:27.967
and how to express
my intentions more clearly.

56:28.635 --> 56:29.886
I'm sorry.

56:30.470 --> 56:32.847
I know it's easy to judge

56:32.931 --> 56:34.933
and talk about someone's finished work.

56:35.016 --> 56:37.352
But don't underestimate
the pain and effort

56:37.435 --> 56:39.437
that go into creating the work.

56:40.355 --> 56:42.273
I never did.

56:43.024 --> 56:44.734
I'm not a famous writer.

56:45.360 --> 56:47.529
My books don't sell well.

56:47.612 --> 56:49.405
But I have my pride.

56:50.073 --> 56:53.743
At least I have a belief
that my writings and drawings

56:53.827 --> 56:56.913
will have a positive and warm influence

56:56.996 --> 56:59.374
on the children who read them. Got it?

57:00.834 --> 57:02.710
Of course. I'll keep that in mind.

57:03.294 --> 57:04.838
Okay, that's good.

57:07.340 --> 57:09.551
Gosh, Tae-kyung.

57:11.970 --> 57:13.012
Tae-kyung.

57:14.848 --> 57:15.932
Tae-kyung.

57:16.891 --> 57:18.393
You can't leave like this.

57:18.977 --> 57:20.770
What do you want me to do then?

57:23.481 --> 57:24.774
I'm…

57:26.109 --> 57:27.694
really sorry.

57:29.320 --> 57:30.447
Please forgive me.

57:51.342 --> 57:52.802
Oh, my.

57:52.886 --> 57:54.345
Goodness.

58:04.689 --> 58:06.649
- Oh, my goodness.
- Are you okay?

58:06.733 --> 58:07.984
- I'm okay.
- Oh, no.

58:08.067 --> 58:10.028
- Are you all right?
- Gosh.

58:18.495 --> 58:19.454
Tae-kyung.

58:20.038 --> 58:21.122
Yes?

58:29.589 --> 58:30.798
What…

58:32.258 --> 58:35.011
- Oh, my goodness.
- What?

58:36.179 --> 58:37.931
Why you…

58:38.014 --> 58:39.516
Jin Tae-kyung!

58:40.058 --> 58:42.894
- Mom! It hurts!
- Please calm down!

58:42.977 --> 58:45.647
CHAYOUNG HOSPITAL

58:52.737 --> 58:54.072
Is someone sick?

58:55.198 --> 58:56.491
It's Room 309.

58:57.367 --> 58:59.661
The attending physician is on duty.

59:01.246 --> 59:02.872
So he'll tell you the details.

59:39.742 --> 59:42.370
LEE MYUNG-HAN

01:00:20.783 --> 01:00:24.078
The results from a pulmonary PET scan
and sputum test have come out.

01:00:25.580 --> 01:00:27.290
It's cancer.

01:00:28.041 --> 01:00:30.960
It's stage three cancer.

01:00:31.836 --> 01:00:33.880
If you look at the PET scan here,

01:00:33.963 --> 01:00:37.258
it seems that
cancer has spread considerably

01:00:38.259 --> 01:00:40.595
to the lymph node
and to the right of the stomach.

01:00:44.891 --> 01:00:47.602
He must have been in a lot of pain.

01:01:06.829 --> 01:01:08.039
Father.

01:01:24.180 --> 01:01:26.849
Why are you doing this to me?

01:01:28.184 --> 01:01:29.519
Why?

01:01:32.271 --> 01:01:33.439
Why?

01:01:35.233 --> 01:01:36.984
Why are you doing this?

01:02:10.268 --> 01:02:11.394
Excuse me.

01:02:12.061 --> 01:02:14.480
Has Mr. Lee Myung-han
been admitted to this hospital?

01:02:14.564 --> 01:02:16.691
He had a car accident
the day before yesterday.

01:02:16.774 --> 01:02:18.151
What's the matter, sir?

01:02:28.828 --> 01:02:30.705
- Ki-jun.
- Yes?

01:02:31.456 --> 01:02:34.208
- Get up.
- Why?

01:02:36.335 --> 01:02:38.796
- It hurts.
- What?

01:02:41.549 --> 01:02:43.676
Yu-jin, what's wrong? What is it?

01:02:43.760 --> 01:02:45.511
My stomach hurts so much.

01:02:46.220 --> 01:02:48.473
What's wrong, Yu-jin?

01:02:49.849 --> 01:02:50.725
What…

01:02:53.019 --> 01:02:56.564
The rain said to the wind…

01:02:58.316 --> 01:03:00.985
What's your relationship with Mr. Lee?

01:03:03.029 --> 01:03:04.363
I'm his guardian.

01:03:05.740 --> 01:03:06.949
I'm from the police.

01:03:07.784 --> 01:03:10.244
An arrest warrant
has been issued for Mr. Lee

01:03:10.328 --> 01:03:12.830
for self-inflicted injury and blackmail,
and insurance fraud.

01:03:37.146 --> 01:03:39.065
"You push."

01:03:40.107 --> 01:03:41.234
"And I'll…

01:03:42.777 --> 01:03:44.278
pour."

01:04:12.306 --> 01:04:13.349
You learn more

01:04:14.100 --> 01:04:17.603
when you get things wrong
rather than when you get them right.

01:04:17.687 --> 01:04:20.898
Do you know what
the stupidest thing in the world is?

01:04:21.566 --> 01:04:23.359
Breaking up out of love.

01:04:24.610 --> 01:04:25.903
Don't let Si-woo go.

01:04:25.987 --> 01:04:28.573
Not for him but for yourself.

01:04:30.032 --> 01:04:32.827
Because it's you, Jin Ha-kyung.

01:04:34.203 --> 01:04:36.914
Because it's you, Lee Si-woo.

01:04:39.250 --> 01:04:42.044
Because I just like you.

01:04:42.545 --> 01:04:44.255
Because I like being with you.

01:04:46.382 --> 01:04:51.053
Subtitle translation by: Soo-hyun Yang
